    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Report a bug: <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/GBrowser/issues">github.com/edgafner/GBrowser/issues</a></p>
        <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:jgafner@dorkag.com">jgafner@dorkag.com</a></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Solve common GBrowser problems, learn which data GBrowser sends and stores, and report a bug or contact the author.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Fix common problems, report a bug or contact the author.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Troubleshoot GBrowser in JetBrains IDEs: blank tool window and JCEF errors, sites that block embedded browsers, cookies and shortcuts, privacy, and how to report a bug.</web-summary>

    <p>
        This page lists common GBrowser problems and their solutions, the data GBrowser sends and stores, and how to report a bug or contact the author.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Common problems" id="common-problems">
        <chapter title="The tool window stays blank" id="blank-tool-window">
            <p>
                GBrowser needs the IDE's embedded Chromium browser (JCEF).
                Check that the bundled <control>Web Browser (JCEF)</control> plugin is enabled in <ui-path>Settings | Plugins | Installed</ui-path>,
                and that the IDE runs on the bundled JetBrains Runtime.
                Then restart the IDE.
                See <a href="GBrowser-Installation.topic" anchor="requirements"/>.
            </p>
            <p>
                The same checks apply when the IDE reports the error <code>JCEF is not supported in this env or failed to initialize</code>.
                To check or switch the runtime, press <shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+A</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ⇧ A</shortcut>)
                and run <control>Choose Boot Java Runtime for the IDE…</control>.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="A site blocks GBrowser or keeps showing a check" id="site-blocks-browser">
            <p>
                Some sites refuse to work in embedded browsers.
                GBrowser has built-in compatibility handling for perplexity.ai, Cloudflare checks, ChatGPT and claude.ai;
                see <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="browser-compatibility-mode">Browser Compatibility Mode</a>.
                You can add other domains to <control>Compatible sites</control> and open the site in a new tab,
                but this does not change the User-Agent that GBrowser sends to that site, so it may not help.
                If the site still blocks GBrowser, use <control>Open in Default Browser</control> (<shortcut>Ctrl+O</shortcut>).
            </p>
            <!-- planned-image src="gbrowser_add_compat_site.png" alt="Add Anti-Detection Site dialog with a domain entered" -->
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="A page shows an error" id="page-error">
            <p>
                When a page cannot be loaded, GBrowser shows an error page with the error and the address.
                Check the address, your network connection, and, for a local server, that the server is running.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="You were signed out of sites" id="signed-out">
            <p>
                <control>Clear Cookies</control> deletes all cookies of the IDE's embedded browser;
                see <a href="GBrowser-Bookmarks-and-History.topic" anchor="clear"/>.
                Sign in again.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="A shortcut runs a different action" id="shortcut-conflict">
            <p>
                Several GBrowser shortcuts are also assigned to IDE actions.
                Assign a different shortcut in <ui-path>Settings | Keymap</ui-path>.
                See <a href="GBrowser-Keyboard-Shortcuts.topic"/>.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Device emulation reports an error" id="emulation-error">
            <p>
                The <control>Emulation device error</control> notification means that no browser tab is open.
                Open a tab in the GBrowser tool window and turn on device emulation again.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Links open in a separate window" id="links-open-window">
            <p>
                Links that a page opens in a new window open in a separate window while <control>Life Span in new tab</control> is on, which is the default.
                To open them in a new GBrowser tab, clear the option in <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="search-settings">Search Settings</a> and try the link again.
            </p>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Data and privacy" id="privacy">
        <list>
            <li>
                GBrowser loads site icons from Google's favicon service, which receives the domain names of the pages you visit and bookmark.
            </li>
            <li>
                To get page titles, GBrowser can also request a page directly from the IDE, outside the embedded browser and without its cookies.
                It does this for new tabs and for pages that you bookmark from the page context menu.
            </li>
            <li>
                When <control>Enable suggestion search</control> is on, the text you type in the address field is sent to Google to get suggestions.
                The option is off by default.
            </li>
            <li>
                Settings, bookmarks, history and request headers are stored in the project, in <path>.idea/gbrowsers.xml</path>.
                See <a href="GBrowser-Settings-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="storage"/>.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Report a bug or request a feature" id="gbrowser_feature_request_and_bug">
        <p>
            GBrowser is open source.
            Report bugs and request features in the <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/GBrowser/issues">GBrowser issue tracker on GitHub</a>.
            Include your IDE version, the GBrowser version, your operating system and the steps to reproduce the problem.
        </p>
        <p>
            If the IDE shows a GBrowser error, open the error details and click <control>Report Exception</control>.
            This opens a new GitHub issue with the error details filled in.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Contact" id="contact_me">
        <p>
            For other questions, write to <a href="mailto:jgafner@dorkag.com">jgafner@dorkag.com</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

